So I enter the shop on DLvl 2, and spot a tin wand in the corner. Aha, I 
think to myself, I'll engrave-test it. (Mistake #1: not thinking hard 
enough.)

   You may wish for an object.

Oh. Seriously? Cool --- gray dragon scale mail, please!

   r - gray dragon scale mail
   "Ahem! Usage fee, 500 zorkmids."

Oops. I only have 328. Well, that's a pain. Maybe I can sell off a bunch
of this stuff... (hocks his wizard's starting kit) yes, there we are at 
600-something. Fine. But what's this? I owe $1000 --- 500 for the 
engraving, plus 500 for this wand that I really, really want to take
home with me!

   Well, I get an idea. If I can buy the wand, I can wish up enough 
expensive stuff to pay off the other fee. So (Mistake #2: not thinking 
hard enough.) I wish up another GDSM, which turns out better than the 
first. I sell the first for 600 zorkmids. Now I have more than a thousand
zorkmids, and I'm ready to pay for the wand.

     'p'
     You pay Akalapi 1000 zorkmids for the use of merchandise.
     You don't have enough gold to buy the item you picked.

*grggkrkkr*  This game is evil.

   So I resign myself to a life on the lam (Mistake #3: not thinking hard 
enough), and zap the wand again, trying for a wand of teleport.

     Nothing happens.

*grggkrkkr*

   Of course, this is actually a /good/ thing, I realize a short while 
later, since it means I no longer want the empty wand. I can just drop
it and leave.

Extricating his paw with difficulty from the nut jar,
